# Each relation below has its own reason; they cover different packages.
#
# Breaks: cuems-common (<< 1.3.1~). Feature 011 (D4, research R3): a
# cuems-common without the /etc/cuems handover ships
# /etc/cuems/network_map.{xml,xsd} as conffiles. This package installs the
# current network_map.xsd into /etc/cuems from postinst on every configure, so
# such a cuems-common left beside it would record that file as its own
# modified conffile and prompt or park a .dpkg-dist on its next upgrade.
# Breaks makes apt upgrade the pair together. No Replaces goes with it:
# nothing under /etc is in this package's manifest (D5), so there is no file
# overlap with cuems-common for a Replaces to license. Feature 016: the bound
# was (<< 1.3.0-23~), but cuems-common 1.3.0-23, -24 and -25 were then
# RELEASED from its debian/bookworm line WITHOUT the handover, and that bound
# admitted them. The handover ships in 1.3.1-1, so the bound moves with the
# version.
#
# Replaces: cuems-engine (<< 0.1.0rc6-2~). 0.1.0rc15 (PR #14):
# /usr/lib/cuems/bin/cffi-gen-src moved from cuems-engine to this package.
# Without Replaces, dpkg aborts on the file conflict when an engine older than
# 0.1.0rc6-2 is installed. No Breaks goes with it, as released (feature 017,
# Q6): engine 0.1.1-1 depends on cuems-utils (>= 0.1.1), so apt upgrades the
# two together, and engines from 0.1.0rc6-2 on no longer ship the file.
# Relation row 26 in specs/017-release-line-reconciliation/.
Breaks: cuems-common (<< 1.3.1~)
Replaces: cuems-engine (<< 0.1.0rc6-2~)
Description: Cuems utils
 Cuems utils is a set of utilities to work with the cuems project